==Trivia==
*Her snakes appear to be reused and recolored assets from [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|Medusa Cat]].
*Her name is a portmanteau of ''[[wikipedia:Medusa|Medusa]]'', the most famous gorgon of Greek mythology known for the ability of petrification, and ''-san'', a Japanese honorific roughly equivalent to English "Mr.", "Ms". or "Mrs".
*Her Japanese name, Madū-san, is a combination of マーさん ''Mā-san'' ([[Mr. Mer]]), ''Medusa'' and possibly 魔 ''ma'' ( "demon" or "evil spirit").
*Her description may be a reference to the Japanese urban legend [[wikipedia:Kuchisake-onna|Kuchisake-onna]], who asks someone if she is pretty, then either kills or injures them depending on their answer.
*She and [[Kunio-kun (Uber Rare Cat)|Kunio-kun]] are the only characters whose English names contain Japanese honorifics.
*Her Japanese description is the opposite of Mr. Mer's. Mr. Mer is a traveling stone statue that is alive, whereas Medu-san turns travelers into stone statues.
*She was technically an event enemy for a short time, as her only appearance at first was in [[Empress' Report 4]].

